-- Pedersen commitments, Schnorr, bit and range proofs over the Part 2 words (slice S9, PLAN section 8, Part 3), kit mode.
-- The slots are the slots of examples/ledger.lang with Position := U256 (an amount word) and posWord the identity.
-- The kernel gives Membership after Agent, the DAO prelude after actChoice, the ledger after Position
-- and the zk prelude after posWord. U256 is a kit item, thus this is a kit.txt row. No outcomeSet: isSetSum
-- and isSetUnit are dao.lang definitions and law 2 is not a Part 3 item.
-- The words are the words of test/zktool.c (S9-p2-zktool.txt): cKA = 7 zkG + 11 zkH, the bit commitments
-- c0 = 0 zkG + 5 zkH and c1 = 1 zkG + 9 zkH, and the 32 bit commitments of the range proof of 7.
def Agent : Type 0 := Sum Unit Unit
def Choice : Type 0 := Sum Unit Unit
def D : Type 0 := Choice
def G : Type 0 := Sum Unit Unit
def Position : Type 0 := U256
def posWord : Position -> U256 := fun (p : Position) => p

def flip : Choice -> Choice := fun (c : Choice) => either (fun (u : Unit) => inr unit) (fun (u : Unit) => inl unit) c
def actChoice : G -> Choice -> Choice :=
  fun (g : G) (c : Choice) => either (fun (u : Unit) => c) (fun (u : Unit) => flip c) g

-- The commitment and the proofs of test/zktool.c, each word decimal. schnorrKABad has s1 + 1.
-- A bit proof is ((A0, A1), ((e0, e1), (s0, s1))). range.open is the Schnorr proof of the opening (7, 11).
-- A range row rbNN is (C_NN, the bit proof of bit NN); rangeList has rb00 first (the kernel fold is a right
-- fold, so the range sum is Horner from the top bit, as pedersen.c). rb00Bad has e0 + 1.
